{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChRJ5w4tjNomrYLHK24Hx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `addMonths` in `dates.js`. Dates on the 31st now land on the last day of a shorter target month instead of spilling into the next month.\n\nThe old code called `setMonth` directly. Jan 31 + 1 month became \"Feb 31\", which JavaScript rolls over to Mar 3. The new code sets the day to 1 first, changes the month, then sets the day back to the original or to the month's last day, whichever is smaller. Time of day is kept and the input date isn't changed.\n\nI checked it with a quick script and the results match the comment at the top of the file:\n- Jan 31 2026 + 1 month gives Feb 28 2026.\n- Mar 31 2026 − 1 month gives Feb 28 2026.\n- Aug 31 2026 + 1 month gives Sep 30 2026.\n- Jan 31 2024 + 1 month gives Feb 29 2024, a leap year.\n- Nov 30 2026 + 3 months gives Feb 28 2027, crossing a year boundary.\n\nI didn't run `npm test`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":789,"cache_read_input_tokens":22774,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":789},"output_tokens":347,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"acbe75a8-1849-411b-9ed1-183e64de4712","uuid":"e56f3cc1-78e1-47cf-a510-8bf9d067b890","timestamp":"2026-11-26T09:22:41.303Z","request_id":"req_011ChRJ5vyBWPjEMjtfqCLpe"}
